#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115031 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115202 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bc0be03-9369-508e-9765-8c88871ec20b" :knowledge-point/title "The Range of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"}] :question/id #uuid "9369a037-e52c-5864-b691-297ae956d0f7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4124" :question/problem "What is the range of $f(x) = 5\\log_6(x-1)-4$?" :question/worked-solution "The range of the function\n\n$$\ny = \\log_{6}(x)\n$$\n\nis $y \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nFor a logarithmic function, horizontal and vertical shifts and stretches do not affect the range.\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x) \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115036 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "03c91ac6-d580-536d-90a8-dc4bebdcdf7b" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"}] :question/id #uuid "408f7da1-fe32-5c33-9293-01103faf1385" :question/math-academy-id "e-4134" :question/problem "What is the domain of $f(x)=\\ln (2x+4)-2$?" :question/worked-solution "The domain of $y = \\ln x$ is\n$x \\gt 0$.\n\nTo find the domain of $f(x)$, we replace $x$ with $2x+4$ in the above inequality. This gives\n$2x+4 > 0$.\n\nSolving this inequality, we obtain\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2x + 4 & > 0 \\\\ 2x & > - 4 \\\\ x & > - 2\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nTherefore, the domain of $y = f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nx\\in\\left(-2, \\infty \\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115037 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c21c1eca-cf80-56bd-9f44-aab7989cb210" :knowledge-point/title "The Root of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"}] :question/id #uuid "fe3c041b-ffb9-5b10-be4a-8a7bb3469a7c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4135" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x) = \\log(2x) - 2$." :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x)$, we must solve\n\n$$\nf(x)=0\n$$\n\n$$\n\\log(2x) - 2 = 0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log (2x) - 2 &= 0 \\\\\n\\log (2x) &= 2 \\\\\n10^{\\log (2x)} &= 10^{2} \\\\\n2x &= 100 \\\\\nx &= 50\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=50$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115038 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115208 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f6f4cfa-db03-5ae6-9f43-79fd3167c473" :knowledge-point/title "The Vertical Asymptote of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"}] :question/id #uuid "f32fd8b8-7e72-5927-a75f-64237997c175" :question/math-academy-id "e-4137" :question/problem "Find the equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $f(x) = -\\ln(4x)$." :question/worked-solution "The equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $y = \\ln{x}$ is $x=0$.\n\nTo find the equation of the vertical asymptote of $f(x)$, we set the argument of the logarithmic term equal to zero, and solve for $x$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x &= 0 \\\\\nx &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the vertical asymptote is $x = 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "03c91ac6-d580-536d-90a8-dc4bebdcdf7b" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "681f6cce-6a63-504d-a5b9-ef8102cd6098" :question/math-academy-id "q-4115" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{log}(\\frac{x}{2}-1)-4.$" :question/worked-solution "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{log}x$ is\n\n$$\nx>0.\n$$\n\nTo find the domain of $f(x),$ we replace $x$ with $\\frac{x}{2}-1$ in the above inequality. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2}-1>0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-1 & >0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & >1 \\\\ x & >2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $y=f(x)$ is $x\\in (2,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234436 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115208 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f6f4cfa-db03-5ae6-9f43-79fd3167c473" :knowledge-point/title "The Vertical Asymptote of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2fa019a-adf5-5729-8706-0b94847387b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-81990" :question/problem "Find the equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{log}(2x)-8.$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $y=\\operatorname{log}x$ is $x=0.$\n\nTo find the equation of the vertical asymptote of $f(x)$, we set the argument of the logarithmic term equal to zero, and solve for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =0 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the vertical asymptote is $x=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115208 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f6f4cfa-db03-5ae6-9f43-79fd3167c473" :knowledge-point/title "The Vertical Asymptote of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf68e5b4-2db7-530c-8311-106b0c01b7b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-81991" :question/problem "Find the equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $f(x)=10\\operatorname{ln}(5x).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $y=\\operatorname{ln}x$ is $x=0.$\n\nTo find the equation of the vertical asymptote of $f(x)$, we set the argument of the logarithmic term equal to zero, and solve for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & =0 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the vertical asymptote is $x=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c21c1eca-cf80-56bd-9f44-aab7989cb210" :knowledge-point/title "The Root of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e6ba761-66c0-5454-8a49-a1749f6fb11e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81999" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=2{log}_{2}(x)-6.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n2{log}_{2}(x)-6=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{log}_{2}(x)-6 & =0 \\\\ 2{log}_{2}(x) & =6 \\\\ {log}_{2}(x) & =3 \\\\ {2}^{{log}_{2}(x)} & ={2}^{3} \\\\ x & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=8.$"}]}
